# Is this trajectory still collision-free in the planner's CURRENT world?
#
# READ-ONLY: never plans, never moves, never mutates the world. Exists so a
# reactive client can tell whether a motion it is ALREADY executing has been
# invalidated by newly perceived obstacles — nothing in the execution gate
# chain re-checks collision, so without this a trajectory planned before an
# obstacle appeared would run straight through it.
trajectory_msgs/JointTrajectory trajectory
int32 start_index          # check from this point onward (0 = the whole thing)
---
bool collision_free        # cuRobo's verdict: limits, self-collision, world
int32 first_bad_index      # index into the FULL trajectory, -1 if clear
int32 n_bad
# Smallest whole-arm gap to the PERCEIVED boxes over the checked span, so a
# caller can react at a margin rather than at contact. inf when nothing is
# perceived; not a substitute for collision_free.
float32 min_clearance
string message
